{"shortDescription":"China's fuel oil exports, which were mainly for marine fuel bunkering, fell in August to an almost two-year low, customs data showed on Sunday.Export volumes totalled 1.22 million metric tons in August, or about 250,773 barrels per day, down 34% from July and 25% lower than the same time a year ear…","astDescription":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"p","children":["China's fuel oil exports, which were mainly for marine fuel bunkering, fell in August to an almost two-year low, customs data showed on Sunday."]},{"type":"p","children":["Export volumes totalled 1.22 million metric tons in August, or about 250,773 barrels per day, down 34% from July and 25% lower than the same time a year earlier, based on General Administration of Customs data. That was the lowest level since October 2024."]},{"type":"p","children":["Some bunkering was hampered by weather at China's main vessel refuelling hub in Zhoushan, market sources said, but prices of low-sulphur marine fuel at Chinese bunker ports have remained below those at regional bunker hub Singapore."]},{"type":"p","children":["China's fuel oil imports, which typically head to refineries and also to the marine fuel blending pool, totalled 1.3 million tons for August, up 15% month on month and down 11% year on year."]},{"type":"p","children":["Buying sentiment for fuel oil in the third quarter has improved from the second quarter but has remained capped because independent refineries still had crude import quotas to utilise."]},{"type":"p","children":["China's crude oil throughput climbed for a second month in August, supported by stronger refined fuel exports after Beijing eased export restrictions in mid-July."]},{"type":"p","children":["The table below shows China's fuel oil exports and imports in metric tons. The export section largely captures low-sulphur bunkering sales along China's coast."]},{"type":"p","children":["The import volumes include purchases under ordinary trade subject to import dut